ation":"Patterson 559","service_line":"Poly Pipe","report_number":"79423271"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Mitchell Gentry Jr","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"Coolant reservoir had a small leak. ","location":"Shop","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79415686"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Shelly Batts","type":"Recognition","description":"my guys cleared rig floor of all trip hazards, safe job","location":"patt 594","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79415023"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Michael Gonzalez","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"While running casing the collar kept getting hung up on the BOP. Rig attempted to make adjustments but it didn't work. Work resumed and caution was taken while lowering connections.","location":"Key P.U.","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79411272"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Michael Gonzalez","type":"At-Risk Procedure","description":"Driller didn't slack off enough while kicking out elevators causing the riser to catch on the nubbing. Elevators shot off the nubbing violently. ","location":"Citadel 3","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79411031"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Fredy Romero","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"During these months of working with the relief employee, Jaime, we have observed two distinct patterns of behavior in the workplace, stemming from his bipolar mood fluctuations. On the positive side\u2014accounting for 40% of the time\u2014he acts as a competent employee who consistently applies his professional experience. On the negative side\u2014the remaining 60%\u2014his attitude toward work is somewhat concerning; this is attributed to personal and relationship issues, as well as a general lack of motivation or lethargy regarding his duties. These negative behaviors have led to various incidents, as he channels his stress and personal troubles in an aggressive manner\u2014specifically when handling tools\u2014without regard for the consequences, creating a risk that he could injure himself or those around him at any moment.","location":"Cactus-163 / 10 3/4\" Casing Run ","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79409674"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Aiden Brantley","type":"Recognition","description":"the unit stopped working mid job","location":"pulling unit","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79405539"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Joao Demenjon","type":"At-Risk Behavior","description":"Not to keep brining up the same thing. It's just gotten to a point where it's almost funny.\nWe sat in between runs 20 hours. Jaime is clearly having issues with his wife via the phone. We are not on the right floor 5 minutes and he's already calling her, after that he comes out amped up. We use a boom line to bring the tongs from the back of the draw works to the middle of the rig floor where we will then change from boom line to air hoist.\n\nI ask all my guys and some roughnecks to put their hands on the tongs to hold back the swing as I don't want anyone to get hurt.\n\nFirst he holds back with us then he decides this is taking too long and pushes hard ( while everyone else is still pulling back) we the sit the tongs on the floor, he quickly removes the boom winch and throws it behind him without saying a word or look what's behind him, a roughneck was standing there and luckily grabbed it, he gave me a look, all I can do is apologize to him as talking to jaime only has negative effects.\n\nHe mad a few more minutes issues during the run including basically throwing a hissy fit with the elevators and pin because the driller set slips, then came up a few inches so the elevators didn't sit on the handles as I mentioned before. Apparently it took too long for him and he showed his frustration.","location":"Run 500 ft 13 3/8 on cactus 163","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79404891"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Joao Demenjon","type":"Recognition","description":"Ryan Warren. It was his first job with us, I like how much he pays attention. He stopped jaime from opening the elevator doors on the 3rd joint because the clamp was pushing against the slip handle, and the slips were not fully set.\n\nThese are the kind of things I'm always looking out for but missed because it was on the opposite side from me, he not only noticed but spoke up, most new and or experienced hands wouldn't have even bothered to look or say anything.","location":"Cactus 163 run 500 ft surface","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79404279"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Taurino Medrano","type":"At-Risk Procedure","description":"Loop bails no secure on utin basket","location":"Shop midland ","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79403581"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Ray Guerrero","type":"At-Risk Procedure","description":"Driller side hoist was in path of top drive","location":"289","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79402553"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Fredy Romero","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"During the rig up and rig down was realized carefully everything to avoid any incident. ","location":"Noram 28 / 9 5/8\" Casing Run. ","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79402249"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Michael Hancock","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"While making rounds around the yard I noticed that the eye wash holder in the CRT shop was broken as seen in the picture provided due to door slamming. ","location":"Midland Casing CRT shop","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79401806"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Ozwaldo Trevino","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"There was a rattlesnake next to our trailer","location":"451","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79401723"},{"date":"2026-04-16","observer":"Stephen Benites","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"A keeper was not in shackle when tongues rigged up the hoist","location":"H&p267/casing","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"79398596"}